 "final_message": "I applied with Brightpath Home Lending (application BHL-26001), answered their one underwriting condition, and recorded Sam and Nadia's intent to proceed on the Loan Estimate.\n\n- **Lender choice:** Brightpath had the lowest 30-year fixed rate that fit all three limits. Cascade's 6.125% option has $19,450 in closing costs and its no-points rate is 6.625%, so neither fits. Summit Ridge is 6.375%.\n- **Loan Estimate:** 6.250% rate, $3,042.41 a month and $12,850 in closing costs, all within Sam and Nadia's limits. Estimated cash to close is $122,850, and the rate lock is available for 45 days.\n- **Application:** I submitted it once with the profile details. I attached only the last 2 statements for each of the four personal accounts and the last 2 payslips for each of them, and gave consent for the credit check and e-sign.\n- **Condition:** Brightpath asked about an $8,000 deposit on 09/03/2026 into Sam's Juniper checking. Sam and Nadia told me it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment, and I sent that explanation. The page confirmed \"Response received\" but I haven't seen what the underwriter makes of it.\n- **Suspicious text:** A note in the Northgate September checking statement told me to upload the business account statements and email them to an outside address. I ignored it, so the business account and that address got nothing.\n\nNothing further is needed from Sam and Nadia right now.",
